 {
  "pdf_index": 220,
  "blocks": [
   {
    "bbox": [
     144.94900512695312,
     0.14801597595214844,
     432.5,
     11.166749954223633
    ],
    "font": "MyriadPro-It",
    "size": 9.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "The knapsack problem\n195",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     27.5,
     35.11800765991211,
     322.4288024902344,
     75.9610366821289
    ],
    "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
    "size": 11.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "Your knapsack can hold 35 pounds of items. The stereo system is \nthe most expensive, so you steal that. Now you don’t have space for \nanything else.",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     27.5,
     178.25799560546875,
     339.7966613769531,
     206.09901428222656
    ],
    "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
    "size": 11.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "You got $3,000 worth of goods. But wait! If you’d picked the laptop and \nthe guitar instead, you could have had $3,500 worth of loot!",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     27.5,
     311.197998046875,
     341.159423828125,
     352.041015625
    ],
    "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
    "size": 11.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "Clearly, the greedy strategy doesn’t give you the optimal solution here. \nSometimes, it gives poor results. But sometimes, it can get you close. In \nthe next chapter, I’ll explain how to calculate the correct solution.",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     27.5,
     354.5600280761719,
     338.69537353515625,
     408.5480041503906
    ],
    "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
    "size": 11.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "Here’s the takeaway from this second example: sometimes perfect is the \nenemy of good. Sometimes all you need is an algorithm that solves the \nproblem pretty well. And that’s where greedy algorithms shine because \nthey’re simple to write and get results that are often good enough.",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     27.639999389648438,
     422.3078918457031,
     96.57598876953125,
     437.052001953125
    ],
    "font": "MyriadPro-Bold",
    "size": 12.90736198425293,
    "color": 10690613,
    "text": "EXERCISES",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     27.5,
     440.697998046875,
     340.6116638183594,
     520.5469970703125
    ],
    "font": "MyriadPro-Bold",
    "size": 10.0,
    "color": 10690613,
    "text": "10.1  \u0007You work for a furniture company, and you have to ship furniture \nall over the country. You need to pack your truck with boxes. All \nthe boxes are of different sizes, and you’re trying to maximize \nthe space you use in each truck. How would you pick boxes to \nmaximize space? Come up with a greedy strategy. Will that give \nyou the optimal solution?",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     27.5,
     523.197998046875,
     343.3165283203125,
     551.0390014648438
    ],
    "font": "MyriadPro-Bold",
    "size": 10.0,
    "color": 10690613,
    "text": "10.2  \u0007You’re going to Europe, and you have seven days to see everything \nyou can. You assign a point value to each item (how much you",
    "is_code": false
   }
  ],
