 {
  "pdf_index": 225,
  "blocks": [
   {
    "bbox": [
     9.496002197265625,
     -3.6251630783081055,
     242.05596923828125,
     15.166749954223633
    ],
    "font": "MyriadPro-Semibold",
    "size": 9.166999816894531,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "Chapter 10  I  greedy algorithms\n200",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     9.5,
     35.11800765991211,
     196.37570190429688,
     49.957008361816406
    ],
    "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
    "size": 11.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "Here are some things you can do with sets.",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     9.5,
     328.8380126953125,
     191.54774475097656,
     343.677001953125
    ],
    "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
    "size": 11.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "•\t A set union means “combine both sets.”",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     9.5,
     350.8380126953125,
     327.0095520019531,
     378.67901611328125
    ],
    "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
    "size": 11.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "•\t A set intersection means “find the items that show up in both sets” (in \nthis case, just the tomato).",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     9.5,
     385.8399963378906,
     327.74755859375,
     413.6809997558594
    ],
    "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
    "size": 11.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "•\t A set difference means “subtract the items in one set from the items in \nthe other set.”",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     9.5,
     416.3429870605469,
     66.21491241455078,
     431.1819763183594
    ],
    "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
    "size": 11.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "For example:",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     18.5,
     438.8486328125,
     318.6748962402344,
     529.0919799804688
    ],
    "font": "Courier",
    "size": 9.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": ">>> fruits = set([\"avocado\", \"tomato\", \"banana\"])\n>>> vegetables = set([\"beets\", \"carrots\", \"tomato\"])\n>>> fruits | vegetables  \nThis is a set union.\nset([\"avocado\", \"beets\", \"carrots\", \"tomato\", \"banana\"])\n>>> fruits & vegetables  \nThis is a set intersection.\nset([\"tomato\"])\n>>> fruits – vegetables  \nThis is a set difference.\nset([\"avocado\", \"banana\"])\n>>> vegetables – fruits  \nWhat do you think this will do?",
    "is_code": true
   }
  ],
  "images": [
   [
    45.83100128173828,
    64.697021484375,
    289.1910095214844,
    310.2170104980469
   ]
  ]
 },
 {
  "pdf_index": 226,
  "blocks": [
   {
    "bbox": [
     140.05299377441406,
     0.14801597595214844,
     432.5,
     11.166749954223633
    ],
    "font": "MyriadPro-It",
    "size": 9.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "The set-covering problem\n201",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     27.5,
     35.11800765991211,
     67.5609130859375,
     49.957008361816406
    ],
    "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
    "size": 11.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "To recap:",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     27.5,
     57.11800765991211,
     253.67758178710938,
     71.9570083618164
    ],
    "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
    "size": 11.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "•\t Sets are like lists, except sets can’t have duplicates.",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     27.5,
     79.11801147460938,
     296.62158203125,
     106.95902252197266
    ],
    "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
    "size": 11.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "•\t You can do some interesting operations on sets, like union, \nintersection, and difference.",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     27.5,
     118.65100860595703,
     129.6706085205078,
     135.99700927734375
    ],
    "font": "MyriadPro-Bold",
    "size": 14.0,
    "color": 6513766,
    "text": "Back to the code",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     27.5,
     139.11801147460938,
     191.46266174316406,
     153.95701599121094
    ],
    "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
    "size": 11.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "Let’s get back to the original example.",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     27.5,
     156.6190185546875,
     134.83580017089844,
     171.45802307128906
    ],
    "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
    "size": 11.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "This is a set intersection:",
    "is_code": false
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     36.5,
     179.12864685058594,
     272.06219482421875,
     188.12864685058594
    ],
    "font": "Courier",
    "size": 9.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "covered = states_needed & states_for_station",
    "is_code": true
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     27.49700927734375,
     193.11801147460938,
     275.0604553222656,
     259.9630432128906
    ],
    "font": "Courier",
    "size": 9.0,
    "color": 2301728,
    "text": "covered is a set of states that were in both states_\nneeded and states_for_station. So covered is the \nset of uncovered states that this station covers! Next you \ncheck whether this station covers more states than the \ncurrent best_station:",
    "is_code": true
   },
   {
    "bbox": [
     36.5,
